techniques employed. Specifically, tests such as 18F-FDG and MIBG are noted for their sensitivity in detecting the presence of disease, including metastatic pheochromocytomas. Overall, SENSIBILIDAD encompasses both the evaluation of swallowing disorders and the effectiveness of imaging tests in identifying specific medical conditions.", "SECRECIONES:Refers to the evaluation of secretions that may affect swallowing, as discussed in the manual.", "FASE ESOFÁGICA:The esophageal phase of swallowing, which is evaluated directly and indirectly in the context of dysphagia.", "ALTERACIONES DE LA COLUMNA CERVICAL:Refers to cervical spine abnormalities that can impact swallowing mechanics, as mentioned in the manual.", "RESIDUO FARÍNGEO:", "ESOFAOGOSCOPIA TRANSNASAL:Esofagoscopia transnasal is a technique that allows for examination of the esophagus through the nasal cavity without the need for sedation.", "CUERPOS DE CUIDADOS INTENSIVOS:Unidades de cuidados intensivos are specialized hospital departments that provide intensive care for patients who are critically ill.", "TOXINA:Toxina refers to substances that may be used in various therapeutic techniques mentioned in the manual for treating esophageal conditions.", "DILATACIÓN ESOFÁGICA:Dilatación esofágica is a procedure performed to widen the esophagus, often discussed in the context of treating dysphagia.", "BIOPSIAS:Biopsias, also known as biopsies, are medical procedures that involve the removal of tissue samples for examination. These procedures are crucial diagnostic techniques used to identify diseases, including conditions such as FQ. By sampling tissue, biopsias allow healthcare professionals to analyze the cellular structure and determine the presence of any abnormalities or diseases.", "GASTROSTOMÍA PERCUTÁNEA:Gastrostomía percutánea is a procedure for placing a feeding tube directly into the stomach, relevant in the context of dysphagia treatment.", "PUNCIONES TRAQUEOESOFÁGICAS:Punciones traqueoesofágicas are procedures that may be performed to address complications related to esophageal conditions.)<|COMPLETE|>", "REFLUJO GASTROESOFÁGICO:El reflujo gastroesofágico (RGE) es una afección multifactorial que se caracteriza por la exposición del esófago distal al ácido, lo que puede provocar molestias y complicaciones. Esta condición, también conocida como enfermedad por reflujo gastroesofágico (GERD), es un trastorno digestivo crónico en el que el ácido del estómago o la bilis irritan el revestimiento del esófago. El RGE es prevalente entre los pacientes con fibrosis quística, donde un porcentaje significativo experimenta síntomas relacionados. Además, se ha observado que el reflujo gastroesofágico puede empeorar o ser inducido por procedimientos de gastrostomía. En resumen, el REFLUJO GASTROESOFÁGICO es una condición que genera altos costes sanitarios y requiere atención médica adecuada para su manejo.", "ESÓFAGO DE BARRETT:El esófago de Barrett es una condición precancerosa asociada al reflujo gastroesofágico que requiere diagnóstico y tratamiento.", "PH-METRÍA ESOFÁGICA:La pH-metría esofágica es una prueba diagnóstica que cuantifica el reflujo ácido y es la prueba de referencia para el diagnóstico de la enfermedad por reflujo gastroesofágico."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}